# THE REPOSITORY ROOT IS NOT THE PRODUCTION IMAGE BUILD CONTEXT (ADR-0044 s.6). The
# context is a directory prepared by scripts/production_build_context.py from the exact
# Git tree of the recorded commit, with the compiled configuration beside it under
# configuration/. This file exists only so that a mistaken `docker build .` from a
# checkout admits nothing but the image source allowlist -- and such a build still fails,
# because no configuration/ input exists here. No tests, docs, infra, LEAN, logs,
# private runtime area, git metadata, generated staging directory or workstation files
# can reach a build either way.
*
!pyproject.toml
!src/
!src/**
!scripts/production_task_entrypoint.py
!docker/production/Dockerfile
!docker/production/constraints.txt
!docker/production/entry/
!docker/production/entry/**
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
